# Rank 1641 / CVE-2026-25150: Qwik City's form parser wrote every
# FormData entry name it handed into nested objects, so a form field
# named `__proto__.polluted` (or `constructor.polluted`,
# `prototype[]`, …) set properties on Object.prototype for the server
# process (prototype pollution, CWE-1321). formToObj in
# packages/qwik-city/src/middleware/request-handler/request-event.ts
# walked `[...formData.entries()]` with two nested `.reduce` calls,
# splitting each name on '.' and assigning `object[key] = value` -- the
# key segment reaches the prototype machinery unchecked. The fixing
# commit 5f65bae2bc carries the change ("refactor: form parsing", a
# fork merge; read as `git diff <first-parent> <merge>` because the
# combined diff is empty): a new `isDangerousKey` predicate rejects
# `__proto__`/`constructor`/`prototype` at every path position and
# bracket key, the root and nested containers become
# `Object.create(null)`, and the walk is rewritten as a plain `for…of`
# loop.
#
# ATTENTION, prototype pollution through special property names (the
# family of ranks 1518, 1584 and 1613), in the one instance whose sink
# and source both exist and whose chain dies inside the engine. The
# sink is bound: the `object[key] = …` writes lower to
# `__js_dynamic_property_write` and `vyql match` reports
# `code.ProtoPollute @ request-event.ts:414`. The source is not:
# `request.formData()` carries no label, because the Fetch-API
# body-reader binding (vyql/bindings/javascript/
# next_route_handler_request_body.vyql) is gated on
# `dependency("next")` and qwik-city is not next.
#
# Re-measured, 3 x --cache off per side, shipped definitions, the whole
# of packages/qwik-city/src: the vulnerable revision reports 178
# findings / 16 VYQL-INJ-013 and none on the parser; the fixed revision
# reports 179 / 19 with three on the rewritten formToObj
# (request-event.ts:438/445/448), sourced from `request.headers` at
# :58 -- an already-labelled input. The remediated walk therefore
# out-reports the vulnerable one with no probe involved, because a
# `for…of` iteration propagates taint to the destructured element while
# a `.reduce` callback does not.
#
# The engine blocker is one construct, measured to need two changes:
# `.reduce` is absent from `elementCallbackMethods`
# (internal/extract/lowering/lowering.go:216), and the element sits at
# callback parameter 1, a position the machinery does not model. A
# table entry alone routes the receiver's taint into the accumulator
# and the vulnerable chain still reports nothing (measured); adding a
# receiver -> parameter-1 edge beside the entry completes it -- the
# vulnerable tree then gains exactly one finding,
# `request-event.ts:381 (request.formData) -> :414`, 3/3 runs, 178 ->
# 179 findings and 16 -> 17 VYQL-INJ-013. That edge is a new dataflow
# relation in shared lowering, so it is not a mechanical fix.
#
# The destructuring-parameter half an earlier review pinned on this
# path is no longer a blocker: `patternParamBindings`
# (internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/javascript.go) binds the names
# an `([a, b])` element parameter introduces, and a reduce callback
# with a destructured element reports once the element edge exists
# (the fifth block below). Only the reduce edge is missing.
#
# Nothing ships, because no subset of the three pieces is safe: ungating
# the body-reader source alone makes this spec's second block fail
# ("rule VYQL-INJ-013 fired but should not have") and re-sources the
# three fixed-tree rows to request.formData() itself; with the source
# ungated AND the reduce edge in place the fixed tree still reports 3
# on formToObj against the vulnerable tree's 1, because the fix's
# `isDangerousKey` is a sibling function whose comparison never reaches
# formToObj's `prototype_key_guard` context, so the shipped
# protoKeyGuardedDynamicPropertyWrite control cannot emit
# core.PrototypePollutionGuard there -- the delegated-check
# attribution gap recorded for ranks 1372 and 1994. The source ungating,
# the reduce element edge and the guard attribution must land together.
#
# Flip conditions: when the reduce element edge lands, blocks one, four
# and five must flip to expect; block two must stay reject, which also
# needs the sibling-guard attribution. Block three is the live minimal
# pair on shipped vocabulary (`request.headers` is the source): the
# same walk through `.map` reports, the `.reduce` twins do not.

test "rank1641: the form parser walks entry names through nested reduces"
  lang javascript
  file packages/qwik-city/src/middleware/request-handler/request-event.ts
  reject VYQL-INJ-013
  code
  ```
  const parseRequest = async ({ request }: any, sharedMap: Map<string, any>) => {
    const type = request.headers.get('content-type')?.split(/[;,]/, 1)[0].trim() ?? '';
    if (type === 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded' || type === 'multipart/form-data') {
      const formData = await request.formData();
      sharedMap.set('q-data-form', formData);
      return formToObj(formData);
    }
    return undefined;
  };

  const formToObj = (formData: FormData): Record<string, any> => {
    const values = [...formData.entries()].reduce<any>((values, [name, value]) => {
      name.split('.').reduce((object: any, key: string, index: number, keys: any) => {
        // Bracket notation for arrays, notably for multi selects
        if (key.endsWith('[]')) {
          const arrayKey = key.slice(0, -2);
          object[arrayKey] = object[arrayKey] || [];
          return (object[arrayKey] = [...object[arrayKey], value]);
        }

        // If it is not last index, return nested object or array
        if (index < keys.length - 1) {
          return (object[key] = object[key] || (Number.isNaN(+keys[index + 1]) ? {} : []));
        }

        return (object[key] = value);
      }, values);

      // Return modified values
      return values;
    }, {});

    // Return values object
    return values;
  };
  ```

test "rank1641: the fixed revision filters the dangerous segments"
  lang javascript
  file packages/qwik-city/src/middleware/request-handler/request-event.ts
  reject VYQL-INJ-013
  code
  ```
  const parseRequest = async ({ request }: any, sharedMap: Map<string, any>) => {
    const type = request.headers.get('content-type')?.split(/[;,]/, 1)[0].trim() ?? '';
    if (type === 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded' || type === 'multipart/form-data') {
      const formData = await request.formData();
      sharedMap.set('q-data-form', formData);
      return formToObj(formData);
    }
    return undefined;
  };

  const isDangerousKey = (k: string) => k === '__proto__' || k === 'constructor' || k === 'prototype';

  const formToObj = (formData: FormData): Record<string, any> => {
    const values = Object.create(null);

    for (const [name, value] of formData) {
      const keys = name.split('.');
      let hasDangerousKey = false;

      for (let i = 0; i < keys.length; i++) {
        if (isDangerousKey(keys[i])) {
          hasDangerousKey = true;
          break;
        }
      }

      if (hasDangerousKey) {
        continue;
      }

      let object = values;
      for (let i = 0; i < keys.length; i++) {
        const key = keys[i];

        // Bracket notation for arrays, notably for multi selects
        if (key.endsWith('[]')) {
          const arrayKey = key.slice(0, -2);
          if (isDangerousKey(arrayKey)) {
            break;
          }
          object[arrayKey] = object[arrayKey] || [];
          object[arrayKey].push(value);
          break;
        }

        // If it is not last index, return nested object or array
        if (i < keys.length - 1) {
          object = object[key] =
            object[key] || (Number.isNaN(+keys[i + 1]) ? Object.create(null) : []);
        } else {
          object[key] = value;
        }
      }
    }

    return values;
  };
  ```

test "rank1641: the same walk through map reports"
  lang javascript
  file packages/qwik-city/src/middleware/request-handler/form-walk.ts
  expect VYQL-INJ-013
  code
  ```
  export function walkMap(request: Request): any {
    const out: any = {};
    request.headers.get('x').split('.').map((key: string) => {
      out[key] = 1;
    });
    return out;
  }
  ```

test "rank1641: the same walk through reduce does not"
  lang javascript
  file packages/qwik-city/src/middleware/request-handler/form-walk.ts
  reject VYQL-INJ-013
  code
  ```
  export function walkReduce(request: Request): any {
    const out: any = {};
    request.headers.get('x').split('.').reduce((object: any, key: string) => {
      out[key] = 1;
      return object;
    }, out);
    return out;
  }
  ```

test "rank1641: the reduce walk whose element arrives destructured does not either"
  lang javascript
  file packages/qwik-city/src/middleware/request-handler/form-walk.ts
  reject VYQL-INJ-013
  code
  ```
  export function walkReduceDestructured(request: Request): any {
    const out: any = {};
    request.headers
      .get('x')
      .split('.')
      .reduce((acc: any, [key, val]: any) => {
        out[key] = val;
        return acc;
      }, out);
    return out;
  }
  ```
